From 74e343f9fd83c2d6b375d2377ee4fdfa0d0cb2eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomtomnet <tompere8000@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:00:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] virtio-gpu-rutabaga: native-context capsets, fixed blob
 mapping, guest dma-bufs, prefaulted blobs

- drm (native context) and virgl2 capsets next to cross-domain on one device;
- x-fixed-blob-mapping: blobs mmap()ed in place into a hostmem background that is one RAM
  region, so one KVM memslot (as crosvm's fixed-blob-mapping); a blob still mapped at unref
  or reset is unmapped first;
- x-guest-dmabuf: shareable guest-memory blobs get a udmabuf, so a native context can import
  them;
- x-prefault-blobs: a new blob's pages mapped into KVM ahead of the guest's first touch;
- rutabaga's poll descriptor on QEMU's main loop (fence retirement);
- a context-specific fence timeline is the context's own (ring index compared as a byte,
  the context checked).

Split out of the 2026-10-12 snapshot of the fork's uncommitted work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
